<title>CHILE: Chilgener to build Brazilian plant.</title>
<headline>Chilgener to build Brazilian plant.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chilean power utility Chilgener plans to form a consortium in Brazil this week to build a 500-megawatt plant in Parana state, company officials said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The coal-fired plant and a port on the Parana coast will cost about $600 million, officials told a news conference. The whole project is known as Proyecto Pontal.</p>
<p>Chilgener will officially form the consortium on Thursday and take a 51 percent stake. The remaining stakes will be held by Brazilian firms Copel, with 20 percent; Inepar, with 20 percent, and Denerge, with nine percent.</p>
<p>--Rodrigo Martinez,Santiago Newsroom +56-2-699-5595 x211</p>
